Anaerobic Reactors — Chernicharo (@wu-bw4: 0, is #reference, #part-of @wu-sources) { r_1AW64A0Q4V7K5SHSNVJYHNZM6F
Carlos Augusto de Lemos Chernicharo. Biological Wastewater Treatment Series, volume 4, IWA Publishing, 2007. [Persistent publisher reference](https://doi.org/10.2166/9781780402116).

Work the complete book for anaerobic treatment. Connect the conversion sequence, biomass retention, loading and reactor hydraulics with gas, solids, liquid effluent and the need for subsequent treatment. Compare an ideal conversion account with the operating conditions that sustain the microbial community.

The publisher's series is available as open-access ebooks. Preserve this volume's actual licence and component notices. The date matters for standards and newer process evidence; freely readable process knowledge is not a substitute for the engineering controls of an operating installation.

